Subject: [PATCH] quota: incognito storage quota from the profile, not host RAM

Incognito storage quota is a fraction of physical memory, and that fraction
reaches the page through navigator.storage.estimate().quota. The memory it
reads is the host's true installed RAM, so an incognito context reports the
machine Apostate is running on rather than the machine its profile claims.

navigator.deviceMemory does not cover this. Patch 0006 patched
ApproximatedDeviceMemory in Blink, which is a consumer of the memory fact
rather than the fact itself, so the quota path was never touched by it. The two
surfaces then disagree, and a page can read both: deviceMemory says one machine
and quota says another. A contradiction between two values is worse than either
value being wrong, because it needs no reference data to rule on.

Measured on the build host. A profile claiming a 32 GiB M4 Max, served from a
93.4 GiB machine, reported an incognito quota of roughly 4.7 to 6.2 GiB where
the real Mac reports 1.6 to 2.1 GiB — about three times too large, and
identifying the host to within the precision of the ratio.

This matters more than "incognito is a corner case", because a non-persistent
automation context *is* incognito. Target.createBrowserContext, which is what
Playwright's newContext() and Puppeteer's createBrowserContext() call, goes
through DevToolsBrowserContextManager::CreateBrowserContext to
GetOffTheRecordProfile, and StoragePartitionImpl passes
browser_context_->IsOffTheRecord() straight in as is_incognito. Every default
automation session takes this path.

The profile carries the real installed figure rather than the bucketed one
deviceMemory reports, which is what the arithmetic here needs: it multiplies by
a ratio and divides by three, so a value pre-rounded to a power of two would
produce a quota no machine of that size reports.

The randomness upstream applies to the ratio is deliberately kept. It looked
like an axiom A3 violation and it is not: base::RandDouble() is drawn once per
QuotaManagerImpl, the incognito refresh interval is TimeDelta::Max(), and the
settings are cached, so the value is stable for the life of the session and
varies between sessions — which is exactly what real Chrome does. Deriving it
from the profile instead would make one identity report a single constant quota
forever where every real Chrome varies, replacing a fixed tell with a new one.

Narrow by construction: the incognito branch of CalculateNominalDynamicSettings
is the only caller of AmountOfPhysicalMemory in the quota subsystem, so nothing
outside incognito quota changes. base::SysInfo::AmountOfTotalPhysicalMemory
itself is left alone on purpose — it sizes V8 heaps, caches and allocator pools,
and moving it would change timing behaviour to fix a storage number.

Ledger: storage.incognito-quota.
diff --git a/storage/browser/quota/quota_device_info_helper.cc b/storage/browser/quota/quota_device_info_helper.cc
index c711fea..0b469f5 100644
--- a/storage/browser/quota/quota_device_info_helper.cc
+++ b/storage/browser/quota/quota_device_info_helper.cc
@@ -4,6 +4,8 @@
 
 #include "storage/browser/quota/quota_device_info_helper.h"
 
+#include "base/apostate/profile.h"
+
 #include "base/byte_size.h"
 #include "base/metrics/histogram_macros.h"
 
@@ -19,6 +21,29 @@ int64_t QuotaDeviceInfoHelper::AmountOfTotalDiskSpace(
 }
 
 uint64_t QuotaDeviceInfoHelper::AmountOfPhysicalMemory() const {
+  // Incognito storage quota is a fraction of physical memory
+  // (CalculateIncognitoDynamicSettings in quota_settings.cc), which makes this
+  // the one path by which the host's true installed RAM reaches a page. It
+  // bypasses navigator.deviceMemory completely: that is patched in Blink at
+  // ApproximatedDeviceMemory, a consumer of this fact rather than this fact.
+  //
+  // The profile carries the real installed figure rather than the bucketed one
+  // deviceMemory reports, which is what the quota arithmetic needs — it
+  // multiplies by a ratio and divides by three, so a value pre-rounded to a
+  // power of two would produce a quota no real machine of that size reports.
+  //
+  // The randomness upstream applies to the resulting ratio is deliberately left
+  // alone. It is drawn once per QuotaManagerImpl and the incognito refresh
+  // interval is TimeDelta::Max(), so it is stable for the life of the session
+  // and varies between sessions — which is what real Chrome does. Replacing it
+  // with a value derived from the profile would make a long-lived identity
+  // report one constant quota forever, where every real Chrome varies, and
+  // would be a new tell rather than a fixed one.
+  if (const base::apostate::Profile* profile = base::apostate::Profile::Get()) {
+    if (std::optional<uint64_t> claimed = profile->memory_total_bytes()) {
+      return *claimed;
+    }
+  }
   return base::SysInfo::AmountOfTotalPhysicalMemory().InBytes();
 }
 
